---
title: Aunt Polly's Sponge Cake
author: Grandma Gustad
category: Desserts
cook time: 45 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@eggs{6%separated}
@sugar{1.5%cups}
@flour{1.5%cups} (measured after sifting)
@cream of tartar{1%tsp}
@hot water{6%Tbsp}
@salt{1%dash}

Beat egg yolks well, put in 1/2 of sugar and beat well again. Add hot water and flour. Beat egg whites until stiff, add cream of tartar, salt and rest of sugar. Fold egg white mixture into egg yolk mixture. Bake in an ungreased angel food pan at 375 degrees for about 45 minutes or until done.
